{
  "requirement": "Compare each saved observation with the current domain. A changed fingerprint returns `Ok(false)`. The caller checks criterion-version compatibility separately under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.checking_records.version_match`.\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<D: Domain> Validator<D> {\n    pub fn check_inputs<O>(\n        &self,\n        inputs: &Fingerprinted<D, O>,\n    ) -> Result<bool, D::Error>;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `check_inputs`.\n\nObligations drawn from the requirement text:\n1. Compare each saved observation with the current domain.\n2. Return `Ok(false)` when a fingerprint has changed.\n3. Return `Ok(true)` when nothing has changed. This follows from the `Result<bool, _>` signature and is the complement of the `Ok(false)` rule.\n4. Propagate `D::Error` from domain resolution. This is part of the signature.\n5. Leave criterion-version checking to the caller. That obligation sits with the cited `version_match` requirement and needs no test here.\n\nTest mapping:\n- `changing_one_criteria_input_does_not_invalidate_another`:\n  - Two saved records each read a different node. After one node's content changes, `check_inputs` returns false for the record that read it and true for the other record.\n  - This covers a changed `Dependency::Node` fingerprint and an unchanged one, and shows the check is per record.\n- `dependency_resolution_failures_do_not_execute_or_replace_saved_answers`:\n  - The saved record has two observations, a `Dependency::Node` followed by a `Dependency::OutgoingEdges`.\n  - `check_inputs` returns `Ok(true)` while both match. After the edge set changes, it returns `Ok(false)`. This covers an unchanged first observation followed by a changed later one, and the edge-fingerprint kind.\n  - With the domain's `fail_read` and `fail_edges` flags set in turn, `check_inputs` returns `Err(\"read\")` and `Err(\"edges\")`. This checks that errors propagate for both observation kinds.\n- `input_checking_and_execution_keep_separate_observations`: after a node's content changes, `check_inputs` on a loaded record returns false.\n\nI read the implementation (`dependencies_are_current` in `graph.rs`) only to confirm which input classes exist. It has two dependency variants, a changed-fingerprint early return of false, and a final true. Both variants and both outcomes are tested, and so are the error paths. The `public_api` test is unrelated to this requirement's behavior.\n\nI found no gaps.",
